From 5aac3c2adc3f0f9811f3c0d022f6010f63856848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shibco <cade@parare.al>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 20:53:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 95/95] winex11: separate pointer coast sources

Keep direct fine scrolling and direct middle-button navigation enabled, but
make their continued movement independent and default both continuations off.
TouchpadInertia now controls only precise XI2 scrolling. A repeated cumulative
value remains the preferred end hint; explicit enabled mode can also infer an
end from 100 ms of inactivity, with twice the normal starting-speed threshold.
MiddleDragThrow records the raw terminal pointer path, beginning at Button2
press, and evaluates only the real release. A pause, reversal, abort, or chord
cancels it.

Raise the continued-movement envelope enough for the default exponential
curve to decay naturally: 15 units per packet, 480 per axis, 192 packets, and
1,200 units per second. The packet budget remains an independent backstop for
deliberately slow custom rates, and delayed frames are still discarded.

Restore physical discrete wheel input while a stable ordinary button chord is
held. WheelWhileButtonHeld defaults enabled and uses Wine's stock input path
only when the event's button mask exactly matches current Win32 state, keeping
capture and MK_* flags. Correlate XIPointerEmulated smooth reports with their
same-time legacy core Button4-7 copies by display thread, target, direction,
and held-button mask, so those mirrored copies remain suppressed. Smooth
valuator, pinch, middle-drag, stored, and delayed packets retain the fixed-
position button and serial guards.

Finally, make named pointer values case-insensitive, accept off and 0 for
settings that support disabled, and report malformed values on winediag so the
launcher's normal log shows them.

